the inode is a database that describes the files or directory attributes, such as metadata and the physicacl location on the hard drive.
links:
hard links: a synced carbon copy of a file that refers directly to the inode of a file, it points to the same storage space or to the same inode where the content is present.
$ ln file1.txt hard_link_file1          //create a hard link
$ ls -i                                 //show the inode
